 ## Background
-The Extended Cube Architecture was developed as an extension of the original Cube architecture, which was a special-purpose computer architecture for volume visualization supporting only orthographic projection [S1]. The original Cube used a Cubic Frame Buffer (CFB) and beam projection mechanisms [S1]. Arbitrary parallel projections were previously created by rotating the scene and viewing it through a principal orthographic direction, but this distorted the CFB image [S1]. The extended architecture was presented to support real-time arbitrary viewing without distortion [S1]. It builds on the Cube-3 Hybrid Ray-Casting method [3143-cube-3-hybrid-ray-casting.md].
